### Important HTML Tags Highlighted

| Tag           | Purpose                                                 | Notes                                                                                   |
|---------------|---------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `<!DOCTYPE html>` | Declares the document type and version                 | Informs browser this is an HTML5 document                                               |
| `<html>`      | Root element of an HTML document                         | Contains `<head>` and `<body>`                                                          |
| `<head>`      | Contains metadata like title, favicon, and meta tags    | Not visible on the page                                                                 |
| `<body>`      | Contains visible page content                            | Includes headings, paragraphs, images, etc.                                            |
| `<title>`     | Sets the page title displayed on browser tab             | Must be inside `<head>`                                                                 |
| `<h1>, <h2>`  | Headings with hierarchical importance                   | Size can be styled with CSS, importance is semantic                                    |
| `<meta charset="UTF-8">` | Specifies character encoding                        | Important for supporting special characters and emojis                                 |
| `<meta name="viewport">` | Controls layout on mobile devices                   | Essential for responsive web design                                                    |
| `<address>`   | Contains contact or address information                  | Helps search engines understand address data                                           |
| `<link rel="icon">` | Adds favicon icon to browser tab                      | Improves user experience and branding                                                  |

